==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Jeanne, type ψ''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Jeanne ψ''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Jeanne is an excellent unit to use against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies. With all [[Blood Fruit]] and [[Sky Fruit]] Treasures at 100%, Jeanne has an amazing 23,208 DPS against said traits, along with a rather small blind spot and piercing range. When dealing with Red enemies, she can be used to snipe [[Professor A.]], has enough speed to counter [[Hackey]], while her Long Distance lets her hit layered crowds of [[Capy|Capies]] and peons like [[Ginger Snache]]s. When it comes to Floating enemies, she can easily deal with crowds of [[Pigeon de Sable]]s, [[Brollow]]s, [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s and even [[Gobble]]s, under the right circumstances.

For general use, however, her performance is far more limited. Her stats are below par outside of her targeted traits, and she only has 400 standing range with only a bit of piercing, though still decent to bring on levels with a tough frontline where she can be used to target the backline due to her decent Long Distance DPS. Enemies that outrange her easily, such as [[Othom]], can also hinder her use on various stages.

==='''True Form'''===
The basic stat improvements are self-explanatory, and more than a good enough reason to aim for this True Form on their own. However, [[Colossus Slayer]] and [[Immune to Explosions|Explosion]]/[[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]] grant her new matchups against a few notable enemies.

Colossus Slayer sees its best use against [[Baron Seal]] and [[J.J. Jackrabbit]] where it can let her dish out an unfathomably high 188k DPH at Lv.50, and at blazing 2.9-second attack rate. This makes her an even better pick for [[Baron Seal Strikes]] than she was before, while also allowing her to eliminate a 200% magnification J.J. Jackrabbit in a single hit. Against [[Mega-Mooth]], things aren't as favorable since she's outranged by its Omni Strike, which is a death sentence for most units, including Divine Jeanne ψ. However, it is possible for Jeanne to use other enemies as stepping stones to snipe the boss if there are truly no better options. She isn't too great for most other [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossi]], due to a combination of the supporting threats that render her usage questionable at best.

Finally, Explosion/Freeze Immunity are only applicable for a few enemies at the current moment. Notably, Explosion Immunity makes her one of the best picks for [[Journey to Talent (Bahamut Cat)|Bahamut's Talent Stage]], if you're struggling on that. Additionally, Explosion Immune can help her stay alive against [[Poultrio]] for longer, though you will need to keep Poultrio stalled well since Jeanne only has a 10 range advantage over their Omni Strikes. However, [[Le'Prude|Le'Prude's]] maximum range matches Jeanne's own, preventing her from being as useful as she could be against him. Freeze Immunity is primarily useful for mixed stages featuring [[Henry]], who is a hard-counter to most backliners, but can also be used reliably against [[CTO Seal]] whenever relevant. So, while nothing flashy, Jeanne's True Form is a good improvement to her arsenal.

