==Trivia==
*Prior to English [[Version 15.2 Update|Version 15.2]], Jeanne's Normal Form was named Headmistress Jeanne, and her Evolved Form was named Headmistress Jeanne, type ψ.
**In the patch notes for Version 15.2, Jeanne was still referred to with her old title.
**Drop lists for [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] events that include Jeanne were also not updated to use her new names until the introduction of [[Raclesa (Uber Rare Cat)|Raclesa]] several weeks later.
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], Her, [[Raclesa (Uber Rare Cat)|Raclesa]], [[Pegasa (Uber Rare Cat)|Pegasa]], [[Terun (Uber Rare Cat)|Terun]] and [[Lilin (Uber Rare Cat)|Lilin]]'s Evolved Forms were missing the ", type" part of their names that other Galaxy Gals had.
*Headmistress Jeanne, Huntress Terun and Raclesa the Lioness were the only Galaxy Gals to have titles in their English names, prior to Jeanne's and Raclesa's being removed in BCEN Version 15.2 and Terun's being removed in Ver. 15.3.
*The ψ in her Evolved Form's name is the Greek letter "Psi".
*She is the only Galaxy Gal whose Normal Form is in full color.
*Jeanne and [[Musashi Miyamoto (Legend Rare Cat)|Musashi Miyamoto]] were the first units to have the [[Insane Damage]] ability.
*Jeanne could be a reference to [[wikia:typemoon:Jeanne d'Arc|Jeanne d'Arc]] from the [[wikia:typemoon:Fate series|Fate franchise]] due to using a flagpole as a weapon, similarly to Jeanne d'Arc's noble phantasm [[wikia:typemoon:Luminosité Eternelle|Luminosité Eternelle]]. Additionally, her Evolved Form bears a personality and color scheme similar to that of Jeanne d'Arc Alter; a ruthlessly cruel and stern side of Jeanne, who is also clad in black and red. Her flagpole also changes from white to black, similarly to the contrast between the two Jeanne's noble phantasms, [[wikia:typemoon:Luminosité Eternelle|Luminosité Eternelle]] and [[wikia:typemoon:La Grondement Du Haine|La Grondement Du Haine]]. Jeanne, type ψ's Japanese description even states that she is another side of Jeanne, just like Jeanne d'Arc Alter being an alternate aspect of Jeanne d'Arc.

